# =============================================================================
# nosend.dev — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
#
# Project:      nosend.dev — privacy-first developer tools
# Repository:   github.com/<owner>/nosend.dev (private)
# Stack:        Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS  ·  Cloudflare Pages  ·  Cloudflare Workers
#               Lemon Squeezy (payments)  ·  Wrangler CLI  ·  Node.js 18+
#
# =============================================================================
# ⚠️  THIS FILE IS SECURITY-CRITICAL — READ BEFORE EDITING
# =============================================================================
#
# A single committed secret can destroy the entire project:
#
#   • Public GitHub repos are scanned by credential-harvesting bots within
#     ~5 minutes of every push. Private repos are scanned too (insider leaks,
#     misconfigured mirrors, GitHub Actions logs).
#
#   • A leaked LS_API_KEY (Lemon Squeezy) grants full account takeover —
#     license issuing, customer data, revenue-model collapse.
#
#   • A leaked .dev.vars exposes the same key to anyone with repo access.
#
#   • Once a secret lands in Git history, `git rm` does NOT remove it.
#     The only safe response is: (1) rotate the secret immediately,
#     (2) purge history with `git filter-repo` / BFG, (3) force-push
#     every branch, (4) audit access logs.
#
# See README.md → "🔒 Security Notes" for the full incident-response
# procedure. See the "SECRETS" section below for the mandatory patterns.
#
# =============================================================================
# RULES FOR EDITING THIS FILE
# =============================================================================
#
#   1. NEVER delete a rule under "SECRETS" or "CLOUDFLARE WRANGLER" without
#      a security review. Those two sections are the last line of defense.
#
#   2. NEVER add a `!` negation rule that re-includes a secret path.
#
#   3. NEVER ignore `public/` — it is the Cloudflare Pages deploy root and
#      MUST stay tracked. Ignoring it breaks every deploy.
#
#   4. NEVER ignore `_template/`, `docs/`, `worker/wrangler.toml`, or any
#      `.html` / `.css` / `.js` file under `public/` — all are source.
#
#   5. When adding a new tool (npm dependency, build tool, framework),
#      add its cache/output patterns in the correct section below.
#
#   6. Verify before every commit:
#        git status --ignored     → confirm expected files are ignored
#        git check-ignore -v .env → confirm the rule that matches
#
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 🔴 1. SECRETS & CREDENTIALS — MANDATORY, DO NOT REMOVE
# =============================================================================
#
# Any file in this section MUST NEVER be tracked. If any of these appears in
# `git status` as untracked, fix the pattern — do not `git add` it.
#
# What leaks if this section is broken:
#   .env / .env.*     → general environment secrets
#   .dev.vars         → LS_API_KEY (Lemon Squeezy)          ← CATASTROPHIC
#   .dev.vars.*       → variants of the above
#   *.pem / *.key     → TLS / signing private keys
#   secrets.json      → arbitrary secret bundles
#
# All of these patterns below are anchored to reject ONLY the secret files,
# never the legitimate source files that contain the substring "env" or "key"
# (e.g., public/assets/js/license.js must remain tracked).
# =============================================================================

# --- Environment files ---
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.staging
.env.test
!.env.example

# --- Cloudflare Wrangler local secrets (CRITICAL — LS_API_KEY) ---
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
worker/.dev.vars
worker/.dev.vars.*

# --- Private keys, certificates, keystores ---
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
*.cer
*.crt
*.der
!*.crt.example
!*.pem.example

# --- Cloud provider & service credentials ---
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account.json
*-credentials.json
*-service-account.json
google-services.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json

# --- Token files, CLI auth caches ---
.npmrc.local
.yarnrc.local
.pypirc
.netrc
.authinfo
*.token
*token.txt
*secrets*.json
*secret*.yaml
*secret*.yml
!src/**/*secrets*.ts
!public/**/*secret*.html

# --- Wrangler account cache (contains session tokens) ---
.wrangler/accounts/
.mf/accounts/


# =============================================================================
# 🔴 2. CLOUDFLARE WRANGLER (Workers & Pages local tooling)
# =============================================================================
#
# `.wrangler/` holds local Wrangler state: KV/D1/R2 emulation, build cache,
# and — most importantly — secrets loaded by `wrangler dev` from `.dev.vars`.
# It is regenerated on demand and MUST NEVER be tracked.
#
# `.mf/` and `.miniflare/` are Miniflare's local storage directories, used
# internally by `wrangler dev` to emulate Cloudflare services. Same rule:
# never track, always regenerate.
#
# Note: `worker/wrangler.toml` is explicitly NOT ignored — it is source
# configuration and MUST be tracked. Only `.wrangler.toml.bak` (backups)
# is excluded.
# =============================================================================

# --- Wrangler state directories ---
.wrangler/
.wrangler.toml.bak
worker/.wrangler/
worker/.wrangler.toml.bak

# --- Miniflare local storage ---
.mf/
.miniflare/
worker/.mf/
worker/.miniflare/

# --- Wrangler Pages local state ---
.wrangler/pages/
worker/.wrangler/pages/

# --- Wrangler generated types (regenerate with `wrangler types`) ---
worker/src/worker-configuration.d.ts
worker/src/env.d.ts
!worker/src/env.example.d.ts


# =============================================================================
# 3. NODE.JS DEPENDENCIES
# =============================================================================
#
# Dependencies are installed with `npm install` (or `yarn` / `pnpm`) and are
# fully reproducible from `package-lock.json` / `yarn.lock` /
# `pnpm-lock.yaml`. NEVER commit `node_modules/`.
#
# Lockfiles ARE tracked (they are not ignored here — see "NOT ignored" below).
# =============================================================================

node_modules/
jspm_packages/
web_modules/
bower_components/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-store-*
pnpm-store/
.pnpm-virtual-store/

# --- Yarn Plug'n'Play (zero-install) ---
# Keep required metadata, ignore the heavy generated content.
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions
!.yarn/install-state.gz

# --- npm cache (in case `npm install --cache .` is ever used) ---
.npm/
.npm-cache/
.npmrc.bak


# =============================================================================
# 4. BUILD OUTPUT & DISTRIBUTION
# =============================================================================
#
# ⚠️  `public/` is intentionally NOT ignored — it is the Cloudflare Pages
# deploy root and MUST remain tracked in Git. Ignoring it breaks every
# production deploy.
#
# Only generated, non-source directories are excluded below. The project
# intentionally has no build step for the frontend (static HTML + CSS + JS),
# but future tooling (bundlers, preprocessors, minifiers) may add one.
# =============================================================================

# --- Generic build output ---
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
build/Release/
build/Debug/
out/
.output/
.output-public/
public-build/
_build/
_release/

# --- TypeScript incremental build info ---
*.tsbuildinfo
*.d.ts.map
*.js.map
!public/**/*.min.js

# --- Framework / bundler output (future-proofing) ---
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.vite/
.astro/
.docusaurus/
.serverless/
.fusebox/
.parcel-cache/
.cache/
.turbo/
.nx/
.snowpack/
.vuepress/dist/
.vuepress/.temp/
**/.vitepress/dist/
**/.vitepress/cache/
**/.docusaurus/

# --- Cloudflare Pages build cache ---
.cf-pages/
.cloudflare/
.wrangler/pages-build/

# --- Vite / Rollup / esbuild intermediates ---
*.rollup.cache/
.vite-cache/
.esbuild-cache/


# =============================================================================
# 5. LOGS
# =============================================================================
#
# Log files contain runtime information, request traces, and — often —
# accidentally-leaked secrets (e.g., a `curl -v` dump with an Authorization
# header, or a worker log with an API key in the query string).
#
# NEVER commit logs. NEVER paste a log into an issue without scrubbing it.
# =============================================================================

logs/
logs.txt
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
wrangler.log
wrangler-*.log
*.log.*
!public/**/*.log.txt

# --- Report files ---
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json
reports/
*.report.json


# =============================================================================
# 6. TESTING & COVERAGE
# =============================================================================
#
# Test output and coverage reports are generated artifacts — always
# reproducible by running `npm test` or `npm run test:coverage`.
# =============================================================================

coverage/
coverage-final.json
*.lcov
.nyc_output/
lib-cov/
.nycrc.local
.mocharc.local.*
jest-report*.json
vitest-report*.json
__snapshots__/*.snap.new
__snapshots__/*.snap.pending


# =============================================================================
# 7. TOOL CACHES & INTERMEDIATES
# =============================================================================
#
# Linter, formatter, and compiler caches are transient and machine-specific.
# They will be rebuilt automatically on next run.
# =============================================================================

.eslintcache
.eslintcache.*
.stylelintcache
.stylelintcache.*
.prettiercache
.prettiercache.*
.grunt/
.lock-wscript
*.tgz
.yarn-integrity
.tern-port
.vscode-test
.node-gyp/
.node_repl_history
.node-dev
.node-version
.nvmrc.local


# =============================================================================
# 8. TEMPORARY, BACKUP & SWAP FILES
# =============================================================================
#
# Editor crash recovery, atomic writes, and shell backups all leave these
# files behind. None have value in version control.
# =============================================================================

*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.temp
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
*#*#
.~lock.*#
.history/
.tmp/
.temp/
.trash/


# =============================================================================
# 9. OPERATING SYSTEM METADATA
# =============================================================================
#
# macOS (.DS_Store, ._*), Windows (Thumbs.db, Desktop.ini, $RECYCLE.BIN),
# and Linux (some file managers) all create metadata that is machine-
# specific, valueless in Git, and noisy in `git status`.
# =============================================================================

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
Icon?
*.AppleDouble
*.AppleDB
*.AppleDesktop

# --- Windows ---
