# =============================================================================
# 12. LOCAL DATABASES & RUNTIME DATA (Worker development)
# =============================================================================
#
# If the Worker ever gains persistence (KV, D1, R2, SQLite), local
# development will generate database files and dump artifacts. These are
# machine-specific state, never source.
#
# Currently unused (the Worker is stateless), but kept here so future
# additions never accidentally commit a database.
# =============================================================================

worker/.local/
worker/*.sqlite
worker/*.sqlite-journal
worker/*.sqlite-wal
worker/*.sqlite-shm
worker/*.db
worker/*.db-journal
worker/*.db-wal
worker/*.db-shm
worker/*.dump
worker/*.schema.sql
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db3
*.d1

# --- Redis / Memcached local dumps ---
dump.rdb
*.rdb

# --- Local server process PID files ---
pids/
*.pid
*.pid.lock
*.seed
*.seed.lock


# =============================================================================
# 13. PROJECT-SPECIFIC — DRAFTS, EXPERIMENTS, PERSONAL FILES
# =============================================================================
#
# Files that are useful during development but MUST NEVER reach production
# or the public deploy (`public/`). Uncomment individual lines when the
# corresponding file is actually created.
#
# IMPORTANT: `public/` is deployed verbatim by Cloudflare Pages. Anything
# tracked under `public/` IS public. Never place drafts, personal notes,
# or experiments under `public/` without an explicit ignore rule below.
# =============================================================================

# --- Draft documents and scratch notes ---
# docs/*-draft.md
# docs/*-scratch.md
# docs/*-wip.md
# docs/*-private.md
# docs/notes-*.md

# --- Tool-specific test fixtures (may contain real data) ---
# public/tools/*/test-*.html
# public/tools/*/fixtures/
# public/tools/*/samples/

# --- Design assets not yet ready for deploy ---
# public/assets/img/og-image-draft.*
# public/assets/img/screenshots/
# public/assets/img/raw/
# design/
# figma-exports/

# --- Personal B2B / outreach records (may contain names, emails) ---
# docs/b2b-emails-sent.md
# docs/b2b-pipeline.md
# docs/b2b-contacts.csv
# docs/b2b-notes.md

# --- Deployment logs and personal runbooks ---
# docs/deploy-log.md
# docs/deploy-notes.md
# docs/runbook.local.md

# --- Backup files created during large refactors ---
# *.pre-refactor
# *.post-refactor
# backups/
# _backup/


# =============================================================================
# 14. EXPLICITLY *NOT* IGNORED — DO NOT ADD RULES AGAINST THESE
# =============================================================================
#
# The following files and directories are SOURCE and MUST remain tracked in
# Git. Adding them to .gitignore would break the project.
#
#   public/                      ← Cloudflare Pages deploy root (CRITICAL)
#   public/index.html
#   public/privacy.html
#   public/terms.html
#   public/pricing.html
#   public/business.html
#   public/404.html
#   public/robots.txt
#   public/sitemap.xml
#   public/_headers             ← Cloudflare security headers (CRITICAL)
#   public/_redirects           ← Cloudflare redirect rules (CRITICAL)
#   public/favicon.svg
#   public/assets/css/style.css
#   public/assets/js/common.js
#   public/assets/js/license.js
#   public/assets/js/sdk.js
#   public/assets/img/og-image.png
#   public/tools/*/index.html
#
#   _template/tool.html          ← Master tool template
#   worker/wrangler.toml         ← Worker config (source, not secrets)
#   worker/package.json          ← Worker dependencies
#   worker/package-lock.json     ← Worker lockfile (REPRODUCIBILITY)
#   worker/src/index.js          ← Worker code
#
#   docs/launch-checklist.md
#   docs/strategy.md
#   docs/b2b-emails.md
#
#   README.md
#   .gitignore                   ← this file
#   .editorconfig                ← if ever added
#   LICENSE                      ← if ever added
#
#   .env.example                 ← template (no real secrets, tracked)
#   worker/.dev.vars.example     ← template (no real secrets, tracked)
#
# If any of the above appears as ignored by `git status --ignored`, the
# pattern responsible must be fixed — never the file removed.
#
# Verify with:
#   git check-ignore -v public/index.html          → should print nothing
#   git check-ignore -v public/_headers            → should print nothing
#   git check-ignore -v worker/wrangler.toml       → should print nothing
#   git ls-files public/ | wc -l                   → should be > 0
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 15. PRE-COMMIT VERIFICATION — RUN BEFORE EVERY COMMIT
# =============================================================================
#
# These commands are the last gate before a secret hits Git history. Run
# them, or make them a Git pre-commit hook (see `.husky/pre-commit` if
# husky is ever adopted). Each command has an expected result.
#
#   ── 1. Secret files must NOT appear in `git status` ─────────────────────
#     git status
#       → .env, .dev.vars, *.pem must NOT be listed
#
#   ── 2. Confirm ignore rules match ───────────────────────────────────────
#     git check-ignore -v .env
#       → .gitignore:<line>:<pattern>    .env
#     git check-ignore -v worker/.dev.vars
#       → .gitignore:<line>:<pattern>    worker/.dev.vars
#
#   ── 3. Confirm source files are NOT ignored ────────────────────────────
#     git check-ignore -v public/index.html
#       → (no output; exit code 1 means "not ignored" — correct)
#     git check-ignore -v worker/wrangler.toml
#       → (no output; exit code 1 means "not ignored" — correct)
#
#   ── 4. Confirm no secret ever entered history ──────────────────────────
#     git log --all --full-history -- "*.env"          → empty
#     git log --all --full-history -- "*.dev.vars"     → empty
#     git log --all --full-history -- "*.pem"          → empty
#     git log --all --full-history -- "*.key"          → empty
#     git log --all --full-history -- "*.p12"          → empty
#
#   ── 5. Confirm public/ is tracked ───────────────────────────────────────
#     git ls-files public/ | wc -l
#       → should be > 0 (typically 15–25 files)
#
#   ── 6. Optional: full secret scan with gitleaks ─────────────────────────
#     npx gitleaks detect --source . --verbose
#       → "no leaks found" (or fix anything it reports)
#
# If ANY of these checks fail, do not commit. Fix the root cause:
#   • If a secret is tracked      → git rm --cached <file> + add rule
#   • If a secret is in history   → rotate it, then purge history
#   • If public/ is ignored       → find and delete the offending pattern
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 16. WHEN TO UPDATE THIS FILE
# =============================================================================
#
# Add a rule when:
#   • A new npm package generates a cache directory       → §7 (Tool caches)
#   • A new build tool is adopted (Vite, esbuild, etc.)   → §4 (Build output)
#   • A new editor becomes common in the team             → §10 (Editors)
#   • A new AI coding assistant is adopted                → §11 (AI)
#   • A new local database is used (KV/D1/R2 emulation)   → §12 (Databases)
#   • A new class of secret appears (e.g., webhook URL)   → §1  (Secrets)
#
# NEVER add a rule that:
#   • Ignores `public/` or any file directly under it
#   • Ignores `worker/wrangler.toml`, `worker/package.json`, or
#     `worker/package-lock.json`
#   • Ignores `_template/tool.html` or `docs/*.md`
#   • Ignores the repository root `README.md` or this file
#   • Uses a broad wildcard that could catch source files
#     (e.g., `*.js` — this would ignore EVERY tool script)
#   • Negates a secret rule with `!`
#
# When in doubt: run `git check-ignore -v <path>` before and after the
# change to confirm the exact rule that matches.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
